# Git authorship — no Cursor co-author

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` / `cursoragent@cursor.com` (or any Cursor agent identity) to commits.
- Cursor’s shell may inject that trailer into `git commit` / `git commit-tree`. After any commit made in this environment, verify `git log -1 --format=%B` and strip the trailer via `git hash-object -t commit` + `update-ref` (not `commit-tree`, which is intercepted) before push.
- Do not present Cursor as a co-author on GitHub or in commit messages unless the user explicitly asks for it.
- Author commits as the user’s configured git identity only.
- Only create commits when the user explicitly asks for a commit in that message.
